---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../config/site';
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  metaTitle={`Cookie Policy | ${siteConfig.name}`}
  metaDescription={`Understand how ${siteConfig.name} uses browser localStorage and optional analytics/advertising cookies under Google Consent Mode v2.`}
  pathname="/cookie-policy/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Cookie Policy', href: '/cookie-policy/' }]}
>
  <p>
    <strong>Last Updated:</strong> {siteConfig.lastUpdatedDefault}
  </p>
  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how <strong>{siteConfig.name}</strong> uses browser local storage and cookies, and how you can control your preferences at any time.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6">
    1. Strictly Necessary Local Storage
  </h2>
  <p>
    We use browser <code>localStorage</code> for three functional features that operate entirely on your device:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
    <li><code>buildmath_project_list</code>: Stores the calculations and material shopping lists you explicitly add to "My Project".</li>
    <li><code>buildmath_theme</code>: Remembers whether you selected Light Mode or Dark Mode.</li>
    <li><code>buildmath_consent_v2</code>: Remembers your cookie consent choice so you are not prompted on every page load.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6">
    2. Advertising & Analytics Cookies
  </h2>
  <p>
    Currently, display advertising and third-party ad cookies are disabled by default across {siteConfig.name}. When display ads are enabled, optional EU/UK advertising consent is handled through Google AdSense's certified TCF v2.2 Consent Management Platform (CMP).
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-6">
    3. How to Clear Your Browser Storage
  </h2>
  <p>
    You can clear your saved local storage preferences on this device at any time using the button below, or via your browser settings:
  </p>
  <div class="my-4">
    <button
      type="button"
      onclick="localStorage.removeItem('buildmath_consent_v2'); localStorage.removeItem('buildmath_theme'); window.location.reload();"
      class="btn-secondary text-xs"
    >
      Clear Local Storage Preferences
    </button>
  </div>
</ArticleLayout>
